        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "671310f4-4927-524c-847a-fd4bf5eb02b1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Jefferson, George Cuvier, Daniel Boone, Benjamin Franklin, William Henry Harrison, George Washington\n- Places: United States, France, Jefferson County, Oklahoma, Great Britain\n- Roles: Founding Father, President of the United States\n- Concepts: democracy, republicanism, individual rights, paleontology\n- Events: American independence, Oklahoma statehood\n\nFacts:\n- Fossils in the United States were studied by George Cuvier of France and by Daniel Boone, Benjamin Franklin, William Henry Harrison, Thomas Jefferson, and George Washington.\n- Thomas Jefferson was born on April 13, 1743, and died on July 4, 1826.\n- Thomas Jefferson was an American Founding Father and the principal author of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Thomas Jefferson served as the third President of the United States from 1801 to 1809.\n- Thomas Jefferson supported democracy, republicanism, and individual rights, and he helped motivate American colonists to separate from Great Britain and form a new nation.\n- Thomas Jefferson produced important documents and decisions at both the state and national levels.\n- Jefferson County, Oklahoma, was created at Oklahoma statehood and was named in honor of President Thomas Jefferson.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "848c7f4c-a30a-510d-a163-dd5dffc7882b",
        "text": "Page: History of paleontology in the United States. Sentence: These fossils were studied by eminent intellectuals like France's George Cuvier and local statesmen and frontiersman like Daniel Boone, Benjamin Franklin, William Henry Harrison, Thomas Jefferson, and George Washington.\nPage: Thomas Jefferson. Sentence: Thomas Jefferson (April 13 [O.S. April 2] 1743 – July 4, 1826) was an American Founding Father who was the principal author of the Declaration of Independence and later served as the third President of the United States from 1801 to 1809.\nPage: Thomas Jefferson. Sentence: A proponent of democracy, republicanism, and individual rights motivating American colonists to break from Great Britain and form a new nation, he produced formative documents and decisions at both the state and national level.\nPage: Jefferson County, Oklahoma. Sentence: The county was created at statehood and named in honor of President Thomas Jefferson.",
